    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-82894: the integrand equals 1/(x+2)-4/(x+2)^3, giving the stated logarithm and reciprocal-square term. q-2698: f'(x)=-3(x+3)(x+1) is positive inside (-3,-1); the endpoint values are 3 and 7, so the maximum is 7. q-3615: the partial fractions are 3(x-1)/(2(x^2-2x+3))-1/(2(x+1)); integrating gives the coefficients 3/4 and -1/2. q-83367: the integrand equals 1/(x+3)+(x-2)/(x^2-4x-3), giving the two stated logarithms. q-67070: the sum of the first N positive odd integers is N^2, so N=9. q-108909: the sum is N(7.9+0.5N)/2; N=17 gives 139.4, while the other quadratic root is negative. q-30752: the integral of sin(2x) over the interval is 1/2; dividing by its length pi/4 gives 2/pi. q-80726: the assumed axis stretch doubles x and preserves y, so its matrix is diag(2,1). q-81324: x is multiplied by 1/2 and y is preserved; the source calls this a stretch, including contraction as a scale factor below one. q-38020: x is preserved and y is multiplied by 3. q-12044: (x,y) maps to (x+10y,y), a horizontal shear of factor 10. q-8090: (x,y) maps to (x,5y), a y-direction stretch of factor 5. q-165980: (x,y) maps to (x+y,y), sending the square's vertices to (0,0),(2,0),(4,2),(2,2); option 1 shows this parallelogram. Its image and the source solution image show the same region, with an additional shear annotation in the source image. q-81413: (x,y) maps to (3x/2,y), giving the rectangle [0,3] by [0,2]; option 3 and the annotated source solution image show the same region. q-121717: differentiating gives velocity (2/sqrt(4t+1),3), hence (2/3,3) at t=2. q-121739: both velocity components, 2(t-3) and 5(t-3)^4, vanish simultaneously only at t=3. No earlier submitted answers or grades were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
